**Adjusting Slide Layout**

I'm currently working on adjusting the "Ambiente" slide layout in `App.tsx`. The aim is to shrink those amenity cards to prevent the scrollbar from appearing. I'm focusing on the `SlideAmbiente` component and `AmenityCard` right now. Thinking I need to tweak the dimensions on those to get a good fit.


**Optimizing Card Dimensions**

I'm zeroing in on compacting the `AmenityCard` component. My plan involves dialing back the padding from `p-6` to `p-4`, and shrinking the icon container from `w-16 h-16` to `w-12 h-12`. I'll also consider reducing font sizes if those measures don't do the trick. Further, I might tweak the grid gap within `SlideAmbiente` to enhance the visual compactness. I am also investigating a potential layout issue in other areas of the component.


**Analyzing Component Structure**

I've re-examined the `SlideAmbiente` structure, it has a lot of sections! It's a bit verbose.  Given the goal of avoiding scrollbars on smaller screens, I'm thinking about making the header, the grid of `AmenityCards`, and the capacity/insumos sections a bit more compact. I'm focusing on reducing some unnecessary space within each section to keep everything visible without scrolling. I believe making this more compact, should also resolve the user's specific request to "diminua um pouco os retangulos".


**Streamlining Amenity Display**

I've revised the `AmenityCard` component per the feedback on the rectangles; padding is now `p-4`, the icon wrapper's margin is `mb-3`, and the icon container is down to `w-10 h-10`. Also, I'm updating the icon sizes passed within `SlideAmbiente` from `w-10 h-10` to `w-8 h-8`. Next, I'll tweak `SlideAmbiente`'s layout further by decreasing header margins and grid gaps, and adjust padding in the bottom sections to optimize space.


**Reconsidering Card Styles**

I'm now contemplating layout choices for the `AmenityCard`. My initial focus was size reduction within the existing vertical format. I am now reassessing the design, and I am exploring a horizontal (flex-row) layout. This is a potential way to save vertical space. However, considering the user's specific request for smaller rectangles, I am going to try adjusting the original design first. I will try reducing some margins, as a starting point.


**Implementing Card Refinements**

I've decided to refine the `AmenityCard` component by applying the suggested compactness within the original vertical style. Reduced padding to p-3, and lowered the icon dimensions within to w-10 and h-10, as the user requested. In the same vein, the font-size of the title and description will be scaled down. I'll test how this new card works in the `SlideAmbiente`, since I am already updating the icon sizes there.


**Applying Layout Adjustments**

I'm now streamlining the `SlideAmbiente` component. I've reduced header margins and padding, shrunk icon sizes within the grid to `w-6 h-6`, and decreased the grid gap. In the "Capacidade" and "Insumos" sections, I'm reducing margins, padding, and font sizes, and shrinking icons to `w-6 h-6`. These changes should make the content more visually compact and fit better on smaller screens.


**Modifying Card Design**

I'm now implementing the `AmenityCard` refinements. I've switched padding to `p-4`, adjusted the icon container to `w-12 h-12`, and updated the font sizes for better compactness. I've also decreased the margin above the icon. The card's overall dimensions and layout are now more compact and the changes are live.


**Evaluating Grid Height**

I've added `h-full` to the `AmenityCard` to ensure equal card heights within the grid. This aims to keep the layout consistent across different content lengths. Also, I'm integrating the updated `SlideAmbiente` component to reflect all previous tweaks, while ensuring the grid structure maintains visual balance.


**Analyzing Display Consistency**

I'm now focusing on the `AmenityCard` component within the `SlideAmbiente`, specifically the consistent rendering of the cards within the grid. I'm verifying that all the `AmenityCard` elements are the same size, with equal height, despite the variable content of descriptions. I'll analyze how the flexbox layout is influencing the cards' height.


**Adjusting Footer Spacing**

I'm now focusing on the bottom section, specifically the "Capacidade" and "Insumos" sections, within the `SlideAmbiente` component. I am optimizing the layout and spacing to keep the text more compact on smaller screens and to reduce visual clutter. I've decreased the font size of the descriptive text and am reducing the margin and padding around the elements in this section.


**Streamlining Footer Content**

I'm presently optimizing the spacing in the "Capacidade" and "Insumos" sections. I've reduced font sizes and adjusted margins and padding to create a more compact and less cluttered appearance. I am aiming for a more streamlined layout in the footer for smaller screens. I've decreased spacing between the elements.
